              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Painting over damp walls, caulking over a leak you have not fixed, or installing new floors before solving moisture problems wastes money. Find the source of water and air problems first, repair them, and only then spend on appearance.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying tools one at a time from different brands</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A mix of batteries and chargers gets expensive and clutters storage. Pick one cordless platform with a broad lineup, buy a kit with batteries included, and add bare tools later at a lower cost per tool.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping the compatibility check on smart devices</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Thermostats, locks and dimmers each have requirements for wiring, door preparation and bulbs. Reading the compatibility checker and measuring your door before ordering prevents returns and a half-finished weekend.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring permits and old-house hazards</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Electrical, plumbing and structural work often needs permits, and homes built before the late 1970s may contain lead paint. Check local rules and test before sanding or demolishing, because these mistakes are expensive and affect your health.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Chasing sales instead of needs</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A discount on something you do not need is not a deal. Make a list of projects in priority order, watch prices on the items you actually plan to buy, and wait for seasonal clearance patterns rather than urgent-looking countdown timers.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

